  "experiment": "EXP-052",
  "title": "Shared-prefix capacity for alternating agent types on the RTX 5090 lane",
  "generated_utc": "2026-09-24T18:45:38Z",
  "status": "passed",
  "question": "At max_concurrency 1 the shared-prefix catalog holds one prefix. When fresh agent sessions of different types alternate, does each one re-prefill its system-and-tool prefix, and does raising the capacity to 4 restore reuse without costing a live session's continuations?",
  "answer": "Yes to both. With three agent types alternating, capacity 1 re-prefilled the prefix for every measured fresh session (24 of 24 root, server TTFT 3.78-4.52 s at 11,887-14,199 prompt tokens). Capacity 4 on the published image, and the candidate runtime by default with its sessions named by prompt_cache_key, reused the shared prefix for all 24 (25-token prefill, 0.092-0.100 s). The long-lived session's 24 continuations stayed on private_endpoint in all three arms (0.086-0.096 s). On production, capacity 1 sent 28 of 135 fresh sessions (20.7%) through a root prefill at TTFT p50 8.33 s, against 0.35 s for the 106 that reused a prefix.",
  "decision": {
    "shared_prefix_capacity": "Ship the candidate default: max(max_concurrency, max_cache_markers_per_request), 4 on both mainline profiles (upstream NInfer a140e7ae made the same change). Both lanes inherit it through the pinned runtime binary, which reports shared=4 at startup; no lane configuration names the value.",
    "not_measured_here": "Pressure between four resident shared prefixes and several long private sessions near the 131,072-token ceiling; the lane qualification's durability workload runs on the published components with this default."
  },
  "method": {
    "appliance": "RTX 5090 container lane host (Windows 11, Docker Desktop, WSL2 Ubuntu 24.04)",
    "window": "Production (ninfer-5090-v070p) stopped under the lane supervisor hold, one arm at a time on 127.0.0.1:18099, production restored through its relaunch script with health 200 and the hold released (2026-09-24T18:30Z-18:37Z).",
    "probe": "scripts/agent_mix_probe.py (requests as committed in 89ae8b2; server-log join as fixed in cfdd54d, re-run offline over each arm's own request log)",
    "workload": "Three agent types, each with a distinct system message carrying its tool JSON (the server renders no tool definitions under tool_choice none): 3 warm-up fresh sessions, then 8 cycles of fresh A, C and B sessions, each followed by one turn of the long-lived warm-up A session; 51 chat-completions requests, thinking off, temperature 0, max_tokens 16.",
    "serving_arguments": "The shipped qwen38-5090 profile in every arm (131,072 context, bf16 KV, MTP 3, 16,384 MiB host KV, 4 device-state and 24 host-state slots, 8 private continuations); only the shared-prefix capacity differs.",
    "identity": "Published arms send no session identity (the published runtime refuses prompt_cache_key); the candidate arm sends a fresh random prompt_cache_key per session, as stock OMP does."
  },
